"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"The setup will download the Project64 Installer, please finish it's installation completely and download it to its default path. Also, very important, launch Project64.exe once then close it before moving on to the next step.\n\nOnce everything is set up, the host will need to go to the room you'll be using for your Archipelago session on the Archipelago website. Once you have the room, you'll need click the 'Download Patch File' next to your name.\n\nAfter it is downloaded, open the Archipelago Launcher (AS ADMIN!!) and start 'Open Patch'. It will ask you to select your patch file (.apsnap), then, it will ask for your ROM file and Project64.exe (usually C:\Program Files (x86)\Project64 3.0). It will automatically open the randomized ROM and the Text Client, once the emulation has started correctly, you can connect to the Client.\n\nIf the randomized ROM doesn't launch automatically, open Project64 and play the randomized (you can find it in the same folder as your patch file (.apsnap).\n\nOnce in game, on the Project64 emulator launcher (with the randomized ROM loaded) go to:\nDebugger -> Scripts... -> select the 'ap_psnap_pj64_adapter_30.js' should be automatically loaded in the list but the file can be found in the scripts folder inside your Project64 directory.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
